librubbish

This repository contains a C++ and CMake rewrite of the Android JNI library
librubbish.so. The goal is to preserve the original library's ABI and
observable behavior.

Public interface

JNI_OnLoad registers gete()Ljava/lang/String; on
com/xtc/secretapi/XTCGetUtilWrapper. The original implementation returns
xtc_ok from this method, and this rewrite does the same.

Java_com_xtc_secretapi_XTCGetUtilWrapper_init reads the current APK signing
certificate, computes the SHA-1 digest of the certificate encoding, converts
it to uppercase hexadecimal, and compares it with the supplied string. It
returns xtc_ok when they match and xtc_error otherwise.

The original exported symbols getApplication, get6, jstringToChar,
getSignArray, AUTH_KEY, and ERROR_KEY are also retained.

Requirements

Use an Android NDK with CMake and Ninja. On Windows, the build script finds
the NDK under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk\ndk by default.

Build

From PowerShell:

    .\scripts\build.ps1

The default target is armeabi-v7a, matching the original library. To select
another ABI:

    .\scripts\build.ps1 -Abi arm64-v8a

The library is written to:

    build\android-armeabi-v7a\librubbish.so

Verify

    .\scripts\verify.ps1

The verification script checks the ELF architecture, SONAME, required
exports, and prints the SHA-256 hash.

Dependencies

The original library depended only on Android system libraries and had no
third-party dependencies. This rewrite also uses only Android system
libraries, so FetchContent is not currently required. The C++ runtime is
linked with the NDK's static c++_static setting to avoid requiring a separate
libc++_shared.so.

Device testing

tests/android contains a small integration test application. The optional
test-on-device.ps1 script builds and runs it on a connected ARMv7 Android
device. It is not run automatically.
